# Exercise: i.* (multiplication)
#
# The `i.*` operator multiplies two integers.
# (You can also write `i.multiply` - both forms work.)
# Seq also supports type-inferred `*` which works for both integers and floats.
#
# Stack effect: ( a b -- product )
#
# Examples:
#   6 7 i.*    # Stack: ( 42 )  (explicit integer)
#   6 7 *      # Stack: ( 42 )  (inferred integer)
#   2.5 4.0 *  # Stack: ( 10.0 ) (inferred float)
#
# Your task: Calculate 12 * 5 to get 60.
# When done, delete the marker line below.

# I AM NOT DONE

: test-multiply ( -- )
    # Your code here
    0
    # Do not edit below this line
    60 test.assert-eq
;
